{title: Saviour of the World}
{song_number: 138}
{language: en}
{artist: Ben Cantelon}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F#m]God so loved, [E]that He gave His Son to lay down His life for the sake of us. [D]He bore the weight of our sin and shame. [F#m]With a cry He said, [E]'It is finished.' Christ the Lord overcame the darkness; [Bm]He's alive: death has been defeated.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F#m]We must spread the word of His soon return to reclaim the world for His glory. [E]Let the church now sing of this coming King, [D]crowned with majesty: our Redeemer. [F#m]And He reigns, [E]ruler of the heavens. [Bm]And His name is Jesus, [A]the Messiah.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[D]For He made us a way by which we have been saved. [F#m]He's the Saviour of the world. [E]So, [Bm]we lift up a shout for His fame and renown. [A]Praise the Lord, [E]praise the Lord: Jesus, [D]Saviour of the world.
{end_of_chorus}
